  "text_input": "Patient was apparently alright since 1 week back. Then he developed breathlessness, which is insidious in onset & gradually progressive in nature.\nInitially it was seen on exertional activities, now he feels on rest, associated with nocturnal dyspnea.\nThen he developed cough & expectoration, white colour sputum, not blood tinged, not associated with fever.\nThen patient noticed B/L lower limb edema extending till the knee, pitting type, not relieved on elevation.\nThen he developed generalized weakness since 1 week, difficulty in walking, climbing upstairs, & it affected daily routine activities.\nNo h/o fever, headache, vomiting.\nNo h/o chest pain, palpitation.\nNo h/o hemoptysis, wheeze.\nNo h/o loss of weight, night sweat.",
